-surface test fails when the binding parameter is added to signing.sign_manifest","The published reuse-surface doc drifts from the actual signature"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the context-local signer/principal/push-policy binding crosses the ThreadPoolExecutor boundary (e.g. contextvars.copy_context().run inside run_in_executor, set the ContextVar INSIDE the worker body before dispatch, or pass the binding as an explicit run_job argument), and make the isolation test drive the real app._offload/run_in_executor path rather than setting/reading the ContextVar within one thread.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3906,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["app.py:102 `return await loop.run_in_executor(app.state.executor, functools.partial(jobs.run_job, ...))` — the job body runs in a bare ThreadPoolExecutor thread; run_in_executor does not copy the caller's contextvars.Context","Plan: 'the service supplies its startup-bound context-local signer to BOTH job dispatches' and 'pass signer/principal/push policy context-locally to jobs'","_push_mode (push.py:40, called at push.py:163) is reached deep in the store write path, NOT in the argument-threaded signer seam chain (signing.py:528/587, generation.py:261, transition_close.py:153) — so binding it 'context-local' implies a ContextVar","The prior plan-review cache .rebar/cache/plan-review/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/435c18aa50dc67c45398.json raised this same contextvar/executor-boundary defect"],"finding":"The plan binds signer/principal/push policy 'context-locally' and 'startup-bound', but jobs execute in an app-owned ThreadPoolExecutor via loop.run_in_executor (app.py:95-111), across which contextvars are NOT auto-propagated; a ContextVar set in the app/event-loop context is unset in the worker thread. The plan does not specify how the binding crosses that boundary. The push-policy site (_push_mode, push.py:40/163) in particular cannot be argument-threaded through the existing signer seams and appears to require a ContextVar, so it is the most exposed to silently falling back to the env/default inside the worker.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb07b6886114603e2","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan Outcome ('pass signer/principal/push policy context-locally to jobs'); step 3; step 4 ('startup-bound context-local signer'; 'route the push-policy site (_push_mode/REBAR_SYNC_PUSH) to the context-local policy when bound'); app.py _offload/run_in_executor","norm_id":"ndadf84b85fa1d99a","priority":0.4094,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Service binds the push policy (or signer) as a ContextVar once at startup in the event-loop context; the executor-thread job reads it unset and silently falls back to REBAR_SYNC_PUSH/env/genesis, so a job could push or sign with the wrong binding","An isolation test that sets and reads the ContextVar within the SAME worker thread passes, while the real startup-bound path is broken across the thread hop — the test does not catch the regression"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Bind the signer/principal/push-policy inside jobs.run_job at the top of the worker-thread body (from a value passed as an explicit run_job argument or via functools.partial capture), rather than relying on a startup-set ContextVar in the event-loop context; if a ContextVar is retained, wrap the executor call with contextvars.copy_context().run(...) so the loop-context binding is copied into the worker thread.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY` against a current done-definition consumer, or drop the inline source and accept only the file-path `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` that the hosted deploy actually wires.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["grep for REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY returns hits only in docs/adr/0098-*.md (lines 242, 451); no source consumer exists","The existing override read at `_opcert_signing.py:169` is `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` (a file path), not an inline key","Plan step 5: 'file-path source authoritative; inline REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY unused in the hosted deploy'"],"finding":"The plan introduces a NEW inline env-var config key `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY` labeled a 'compat' source, but grep shows it exists nowhere in the codebase (only in the driving ADR 0098); the actual existing override is the file-path `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` (`_opcert_signing.py:169`). The plan also states the inline form is 'unused in the hosted deploy' and Plan step 5 wires the deployment exclusively through the file path. Adding a second accepted key-material input that no current done-definition consumes is config-surface proliferation / YAGNI.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f88846776fd7e5426","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan Outcome ('exactly one of preferred REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or compat REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY') and Plan step 5 ('inline REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY unused in the hosted deploy')","norm_id":"n85e8b79efeae09a4","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator sets both, or sets only the inline var, i